NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
fdj
- format a Morrow DJ-DMA floppy diskette
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.nf
fdj device
fdj device [ -b bytes ] [ -d drive ] [ -h holes ] [ -i inches ]
           [ -n density ] [ -p sectors ] [ -s sides ] [ -t tracks ]
.fi
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
fdj formats the DJ-DMA floppy in
.i device .
A format writes every sector - a soft-sectored write lays down the ID
header and data together - and then reads each sector back to verify it.
With no options, fdj presents the format menu:
.nf
   8 inch formats:    F CP/M single  G CP/M double  H Micronix
   5 inch hard:       C single      D double       E Micronix
   5 inch soft:       A single      B double
   I  other
.fi
Track 0 of an 8 inch diskette is always 26 sectors of 128 bytes, single
density; the rest of the disk uses the chosen geometry.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
OPTIONS
.in +5
.nf
-b bytes     128, 256, 512 or 1024 bytes per sector
-d drive     drive number 0-3
-h holes     1 (soft) or 10 (hard) sectored
-i inches    5 or 8 inch drive
-n density   1 (single) or 2 (double)
-p sectors   1-26 sectors per track
-s sides     1 or 2 sided
-t tracks    35, 40 or 77 tracks
.fi
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
djformat(1), mkfs(1)
.sp 2
